Sealbot patch to Allied Vision vimbax_ros2_driver 1.0.2: camera clock -> ROS time

Adds the sync_camera_time parameter (default false = original behaviour). When true,
each image is stamped with the camera's own frame timestamp converted to ROS time,
using an offset measured every camera_time_sync_period seconds with TimestampLatch.
All added code is marked "Sealbot patch".

The patched files are already committed in this repo. This file is the record of the
change: after replacing the driver with a newer Allied Vision release, re-apply it from
the vimbax_ros2_driver folder with:

    patch -p1 < sealbot_camera_time_sync.patch

